      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You absolutely should not adjust your warfarin dosage based on what you eat; that is a medical decision only your prescribing physician can make. Self-medicating by changing your medication to compensate for diet is extremely dangerous and could lead to serious bleeding or clotting issues. Stick to the consistent intake of your greens, and let your regular blood tests guide any necessary adjustments to your warfarin dose.",
      "source": "target",
